  "alt": "A software factory separates engineering intent, its encoded property, and a realization produced by the fabricator. Two probability factors annotate the production path: correct encoding, P(E), and fulfillment of encoded obligations, P(F given E). Conditioning on the representation is omitted in the drawing. Agents interpret, implement and correct; engineers authorize intent. The encoded property also supplies a tolerance used in independent evaluation. Measurements from tests, analyses, simulation or human judgment compare the realization with that tolerance. Results within tolerance may be admitted; results outside it are revised or rejected. Production and admission are distinct.",
